==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|who/that ties}}
From {{affix|en|tie|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|tī'ə|a=UK}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtaɪ.ə/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tier (tie).wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{enPR|tī'ər|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtaɪ.ɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|tier}}
* {{homophones|en|tire|tyre}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ.ə(ɹ)}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[tie]]s (knots, etc.).
# Something that ties.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[child]]'s [[apron]].

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|en|leaf tier}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|row; rank}}
From {{bor|en|frm|tier}}, from {{der|en|fro|tire|t=rank, sequence, order, kind}}, probably from {{m|fro|tirer|t=to draw, draw out}}. Alternatively, from a {{uder|en|gem|-}} source related to {{cog|enm|tir|t=honour, glory, power, rule}}, {{cog|ang|tīr|t=glory, honour, fame}}, {{cog|non|tírr|t=glory, honour, renown}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|tî|a=UK}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪə/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|tîr|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-tier.wav|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪə(ɹ)}}
* Homophones: [[tear]] (as in droplet from one's eye)
* {{hyphenation|en|tier}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{sid|en|row}} A [[row]] or [[range]], especially one at a higher or lower level than another.
# {{sid|en|rank}} A [[rank]] or [[grade]]; a [[stratum]].
#: {{ux|en|Stoke City were playing in the second '''tier''' of English football before being promoted to the Premier League.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|system=PC|scene=Turians: Government Codex entry|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Turians have 27 citizenship '''tiers''', beginning with civilians (client races and children). The initial period of military service is the second '''tier'''.}}
# {{sid|en|mountain}} {{lb|en|AU}} A (typically forested) range of [[hill]]s or [[mountain]]s, especially in South Australia or Tasmania; a [[mountain]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Nick Brodie|title=The Vandemonian War|publisher=Hardie Grant Books|page=114
|passage=This party headed towards the '''tiers''' and lakes, scouring the country while veering towards Bothwell.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author={{w|Robbie Arnott}}|title=Flames|publisher=Text Publishing|year_published=2023|page=141
|passage=On she drove, leaving the highway, up a skinny country road, past the snow-capped '''tier''' and into the forest on its foothills.}}
# {{sid|en|comics}} A [[horizontal]] [[row]] of [[panel]]s within a [[comic strip]].

